  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\nAdditionally, under Section 106 of the NIRC, the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) has the authority to impose penalties for violations related to the issuance of invoices, which may include administrative penalties and the potential for further assessments based on the unreported sales or transactions.\n\nIn practical terms, failing to issue a BIR-registered invoice can lead to significant financial penalties and potential criminal liability, emphasizing the importance of compliance with invoicing requirements in business operations.",
